\section{Discussion}

\subsection{Key Findings}

\subsubsection{Development Velocity}
Both projects achieve elite-level deployment frequency with LangChain
performing at
5.97 deployments per day, and Intel XPU Backend at 3.59 daily
deployments. These high rates
indicate mature, highly active projects with robust CI/CD pipelines
supporting multiple
daily releases.

\subsubsection{Code Quality and Reliability}
Both projects achieve elite-level change failure rates below the 15\%
threshold: LangChain at 8.94\%, Intel XPU Backend at 10.58\%. High
deployment frequency combined with low failure rates indicates robust
testing, effective code review, and comprehensive CI/CD quality
gates, demonstrating mature velocity-quality balance.

\subsubsection{Incident Response}
Time to restore service could not be calculated due to limitations in
estimating which issue corresponded with a closed pull request.

\subsection{Project Comparison}

\subsubsection{Similarities}
Both projects achieved elite-level deployment frequency and change
failure rates during daily development and merge activity. This
pattern describes open
source best practices regardless of domain size.

\subsubsection{Differences}
Both projects shared an elite DORA classification, despite
differences in popularity.
Notably, the Intel project achieves 60\% of Langchain's deployment frequency
despite only having 0.17\% of the stars and 14\% of contributors,
suggesting higher productivity
in Intel's smaller corporate backed team.

\subsection{Industry Benchmarking}
Both projects significantly exceed Wilkes et al.'s top-quartile
benchmark of 116.2 annual deployments (0.32 per day): LangChain with
2,180 annual deployments and Intel XPU Backend with 1,310, placing
both in the top percentile. Elite change failure rates (under 15\%)
match DORA 2023 elite performer classification.

\subsection{Practical Value of DORA Metrics}
DORA metrics enable rapid comparison across projects through simple
calculation and standardized classification. Unlike internal code
metrics requiring language-specific tooling, DORA metrics use version control
and project management information. This enabled a simple and direct comparison
between LangChain and Intel XPU Backend despite differences in domain, size, and
architecture. Standardized performance tiers
(elite/high/medium/low) enable immediate project assessment and
visualization, without requiring
a complex exaplanation of the intent and meaning behind the metrics.
Practical applications include portfolio
analysis, competitive benchmarking, and trend monitoring.

\section{Lessons Learned}

Deep analysis of software quality faces a hurdle of complexity and difficulty in
collecting and aggregating metrics. GitHub Actions provided a rich avenue for
code-level metrics, but required invasive repository modifications.
Open Telemetry eliminated
this invasiveness, but required repository permissions. Manual
collection from publicly
GitHub data proved sufficient for collection of DORA metrics, but is
not practical for long
running analysis of large projects.

\section{Conclusion}

This study focused on the capture and analysis of software quality metrics from
two open source projects using DORA metrics from public GitHub data.
Both LangChain
and Intel XPU Backend achieved elite-level performance, despite their
difference in
popularity. DORA metrics provide a simple and standardized metric for
direct comparison
across projects regardless of domain, size, or architecture. This study's
comparison between an AI framework and compilier infrastructure demonstrate
practical application for project benchmarking, comparison, and trend analysis.

Future work should focus on correlating DORA trends with internal
metrics such as
cyclomatic complexity, test coverage, and technical debt to establish predictive
relationships between code quality and production quality. DORA
metrics can be utilized
as leading indicators of quality degradation, and cross-domain
comparison with internal metrics
can be used to trace defects within the system to degredation of
system behavior.

